# Video Editor — Mobile and Compact Entry Proof

The Awtsmoos keeps media, preview, timeline, and transport inside one living vessel;
Awtsmoos.com now preserves full thumb intent even when height is scarce, while deeper controls retract instead of becoming visual wrestle.

## Original measured defect

Before the correction, real controller-driven probes at 320×568 and 390×560 measured Play, Pause, and Cut at exactly 40px high. This came from the short-height rule in `adaptive-motion.css`, not from the main control token. All other major mobile geometry was already clean.

## Preserved working architecture

No JavaScript controller logic, drawer state, timeline math, DOM structure, or timeline scrolling model was changed.

Runtime already proved and the final run re-proved:
- document overflowX = 0;
- document overflowY = 0;
- mobile Media drawer opens fully inside the viewport;
- closing moves the drawer completely off-canvas rather than leaving a visible sliver;
- backdrop covers the viewport while the drawer is open;
- Timeline retract resolves to a clean 54px header-only vessel;
- Timeline minimize resolves to a coherent 150px vessel;
- no transport control leaves a side edge;
- no runtime exceptions are captured.

## UI correction

`css/adaptive-motion.css` now keeps short-height transport controls at a 44px minimum instead of 40px while preserving the compact transport padding and short-height grid.

`css/controls.css` now keeps universal `:active` press behavior while placing hover lift/color feedback behind `(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)`. Short professional transitions connect press/hover state without leaving touch browsers with sticky hover presentation.

A first post-write probe still measured 40px because the isolated Chrome profile reused the old stylesheet cache. A cache-disabled proof then showed:
- measured height = 44px;
- computed min-height = 44px;
- loaded CSSOM contains the 44px rule and no 40px rule;
- a no-store fetch of `adaptive-motion.css` contains 44px and no 40px;
- overflowX remains 0;
- runtime errors remain empty.

## Final mobile measurements

320×568:
- module entry: `./js/app.js?compact=true`;
- overflowX/Y: 0/0;
- Play/Pause/Cut: 97×44 each;
- drawer open: x=0..282, full 568px height;
- drawer closed: x=-296..-14, fully off-screen;
- Timeline retracted: 54px;
- Timeline minimized: 150px;
- tiny critical controls: none;
- off-screen transport controls: none.

390×560:
- module entry: `./js/app.js?compact=true`;
- overflowX/Y: 0/0;
- Play/Pause/Cut: 121×44 each;
- drawer open: x=0..320;
- drawer closed: x=-336..-16, fully off-screen;
- Timeline retracted: 54px;
- Timeline minimized: 150px;
- tiny critical controls: none;
- off-screen transport controls: none.

## CompactJS proof

The real Awtsmoos Dynamic-server CompactJS compiler produced a 28,090-byte bundle from `apps/video-editor/js/app.js`. The generated module passes Node syntax checking. Only after that proof was the HTML entry rewritten to `./js/app.js?compact=true`.

## Source gates

- `index.html`: 89 lines.
- `adaptive-motion.css`: 37 lines.
- `controls.css`: 92 lines.
- JavaScript entry passes `node --check`.
- `git diff --check -- apps/video-editor` passes.

## NEXT_ACTION

Run a lightweight global CSS/HTML risk rank across remaining public apps/games. Prioritize clean surfaces with fixed/viewport geometry, mobile menus/dialogs/drawers, fixed desktop widths, hover-without-active states, or likely unstyled trailing sections. Runtime-probe the highest clean candidates at 390×844 and 320×568 before any rewrite.
